@startuml
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam dpi 150
scale max 2200 width
hide empty members
legend bottom
aggregate root: entry point to the aggregate's entities.
external reference: identity of an object from another context.
Dependencies labeled with Id represent references by identifier.
All value objects have no identity and are immutable.
Values are validated on construction; changes create a new value.
Equality compares attributes, except for Timestamp (UTC instant).
CalendarDate represents a valid date without a time or time zone.
endlegend
title SkyCrop - Diagnoses, Analysis, Reports and Notifications
class User <<external reference>> {
-id: Long
}
class AgriculturalPlot <<external reference>> {
-id: Long
}
class Crop <<external reference>> {
-id: Long
}
class Report <<aggregate root>> {
-plotId: Long
-createdById: Long
-diagnosisIds: Set<Long>
-id: Long
-title: Name
-generatedAt: Timestamp
-type: ReportType
-content: String
+generate(): void
+export(): void
+saveToHistory(): void
}
class Diagnosis <<aggregate root>> {
-plotId: Long
-imageIds: Set<Long>
-cropIds: Set<Long>
-ruleIds: Set<Long>
-id: Long
-generatedAt: Timestamp
-observations: String
-status: DiagnosisStatus
+generate(): void
+analyzeData(): void
+detectAnomaly(): Anomaly
+saveToHistory(): void
}
class TerrainData  {
-id: Long
-humidity: Percentage
-temperature: Temperature
-nutrients: String
-pH: PhLevel
+update(): void
}
class AerialImage <<external reference>> {
-id: Long
}
class TerrainMap  {
-id: Long
-mapUrl: ResourceUrl
-generatedAt: Timestamp
-resolution: ImageResolution
+generate(): void
+display(): void
}
class Anomaly  {
-id: Long
-type: AnomalyType
-severity: Severity
-description: String
-location: Location
+classify(): void
}
class AgronomicRule <<aggregate root>> {
-id: Long
-name: Name
-description: String
-condition: String
+evaluate(): boolean
}
class DiagnosticHistory  {
-id: Long
-savedAt: Timestamp
-reference: String
+save(diagnosis: Diagnosis): void
+retrieve(): Diagnosis
}
class Notification <<aggregate root>> {
-recipientId: Long
-diagnosisId: Long [0..1]
-anomalyId: Long [0..1]
-id: Long
-message: String
-createdAt: Timestamp
-type: NotificationType
-status: NotificationStatus
+create(): void
+send(): void
+markAsRead(): void
}
interface CloudStorageService  {

+saveDiagnosis(diagnosis: Diagnosis): ResourceUrl
+saveReport(report: Report): ResourceUrl
+retrieveHistory(): String
}
interface ImageAnalysisService  {

+process(imageId: Long): Diagnosis
+analyzeTerrain(data: TerrainData): Diagnosis
+applyRules(diagnosis: Diagnosis): void
}
interface MapService  {

+generateTerrainMap(data: TerrainData): TerrainMap
}
interface WeatherService  {

+getWeather(location: Location): WeatherData
}
interface NotificationService  {

+createNotification(diagnosisId: Long, anomalyId: Long, recipientId: Long): Notification
+route(notification: Notification): void
}
interface NotificationChannel  {

+send(notification: Notification): void
}
class SMSNotificationChannel  {

+send(notification: Notification): void
}
class EmailNotificationChannel  {

+send(notification: Notification): void
}
enum ReportType {
DIAGNOSTIC
SEASONAL
}
enum DiagnosisStatus {
PENDING
PROCESSING
COMPLETED
FAILED
}
enum Severity {
LOW
MEDIUM
HIGH
CRITICAL
}
enum AnomalyType {
WATER_STRESS
PEST
FERTILIZER_DEFICIENCY
OTHER
}
enum NotificationType {
ANOMALY_DETECTED
REPORT_READY
SYSTEM_ALERT
}
enum NotificationStatus {
PENDING
SENT
READ
}
class Location <<value object>> {
-value: String {readOnly}

}
class WeatherData <<value object>> {
-temperature: Temperature {readOnly}
-humidity: Percentage {readOnly}
-precipitation: Precipitation {readOnly}
-recordedAt: Timestamp {readOnly}

}
Report ..> User : createdById
Notification ..> User : recipientId
Anomaly "1" *-- "1" Location : location
Report --> ReportType : type
Report ..> Diagnosis : diagnosisIds
Diagnosis ..> AgriculturalPlot : plotId
Report ..> AgriculturalPlot : plotId
Diagnosis "1" *-- "0..1" TerrainMap : resultMap

Diagnosis "1" *-- "0..1" TerrainData : analyzed
Diagnosis ..> AerialImage : imageIds
Diagnosis ..> Crop : cropIds
Diagnosis "1" *-- "0..*" Anomaly : detects
Diagnosis ..> AgronomicRule : ruleIds
Diagnosis "1" *-- "0..1" DiagnosticHistory : historyEntry
Diagnosis --> DiagnosisStatus : status
Anomaly --> Severity : severity
Anomaly --> AnomalyType : type
Notification ..> Diagnosis : diagnosisId / anomalyId
Notification --> NotificationType : type
Notification --> NotificationStatus : status
CloudStorageService ..> Report : stores
CloudStorageService ..> Diagnosis : stores
CloudStorageService ..> DiagnosticHistory : stores
ImageAnalysisService ..> TerrainData : analyzes
ImageAnalysisService ..> AerialImage : processes
ImageAnalysisService ..> Diagnosis : generates

ImageAnalysisService ..> AgronomicRule : applies
ImageAnalysisService ..> TerrainMap : uses
MapService ..> TerrainMap : generates
WeatherService ..> WeatherData : obtains
WeatherService ..> Location
WeatherData ..> TerrainData : provides data
NotificationService ..> Diagnosis : diagnosisId / anomalyId
NotificationService ..> Notification : creates
NotificationService ..> NotificationChannel : routes
NotificationChannel <|.. SMSNotificationChannel
NotificationChannel <|.. EmailNotificationChannel
note bottom of WeatherData
Immutable snapshot without an identifier.
Equality compares all attributes.
The service returns the value; it does not own it.
end note
class Name <<value object>> {
-value: String {readOnly}
}
note right of Name
Non-empty text after trimming outer whitespace.
Preserves the name's characters and original case.
Does not require a specific word count.
end note
class Timestamp <<value object>> {
-value: DateTimeOffset {readOnly}
}
note right of Timestamp
Valid instant with an explicit time zone offset.
Equality and ordering compare the UTC instant.
end note
AgronomicRule "1" *-- "1" Name : name
Report ..> Timestamp : temporal values
Diagnosis ..> Timestamp : temporal values
TerrainMap ..> Timestamp : temporal values
DiagnosticHistory ..> Timestamp : temporal values
Notification ..> Timestamp : temporal values
class Percentage <<value object>> {
-value: Decimal {readOnly}
}
note right of Percentage
Value in [0, 100], expressed as a percentage.
Equality compares the numeric value.
Minimum battery and flight overlap policies are defined separately.
end note
class ImageResolution <<value object>> {
-widthPixels: Integer {readOnly}
-heightPixels: Integer {readOnly}
}
note right of ImageResolution
Both dimensions are positive integers in pixels.
Equality compares width and height in that order.
end note
class ResourceUrl <<value object>> {
-value: String {readOnly}
}
note right of ResourceUrl
Absolute HTTP or HTTPS URL with a host.
Equality uses the complete stored URL, including path and query.
A valid URL does not guarantee availability or access permission.
end note
class Temperature <<value object>> {
-celsius: Decimal {readOnly}
}
note right of Temperature
Temperature expressed in degrees Celsius.
Equality compares celsius; negative values are allowed.
Agronomic thresholds are defined by the applicable rule.
end note
class Precipitation <<value object>> {
-millimeters: Decimal {readOnly}
}
note right of Precipitation
Non-negative accumulated precipitation in millimeters
for the reporting interval supplied by the weather provider.
Equality compares millimeters.
end note
Report "1" *-- "1" Name : title
TerrainData "1" *-- "1" Percentage : humidity
TerrainData "1" *-- "1" Temperature : temperature
WeatherData "1" *-- "1" Percentage : humidity
WeatherData "1" *-- "1" Temperature : temperature
WeatherData "1" *-- "1" Precipitation : precipitation
WeatherData ..> Timestamp : recordedAt
TerrainMap "1" *-- "1" ResourceUrl : mapUrl
TerrainMap "1" *-- "1" ImageResolution : resolution
CloudStorageService ..> ResourceUrl : stored resource location
class PhLevel <<value object>> {
-value: Decimal {readOnly}
}
note right of PhLevel
Finite dimensionless value in [0, 14] for the soil model.
Equality compares the numeric value; updates create a new value.
Crop-specific thresholds belong to AgronomicRule.
end note
TerrainData "1" *-- "1" PhLevel : pH
@enduml
